Subject: [PATCH] fritchii2-listsync: a command entry on pages no GPU work has written yet waits only for the compute

fritchii2-listsync: a command entry on pages no GPU work has written yet waits only for the compute
and copy work sent before the last host-level wait (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSYNC=1); with
EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSKIP=1 (includes LISTSYNC) an entry that begins between methods does not wait
at all while no copy engine work is queued. Both off unless exactly "1"; behaviour unchanged unset.

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii 6baafdd7d9 (the new LIST_WAIT_SKIP shape, EXP41=0 default, released in
fritchii-v5), ported from zortos293/Lichii#805 by jpkto (PR still open): 6229487c8c (wait only for
the writers sent before the last host sync) and d4e8d85d4d (entries that begin between methods
don't wait). Lichii's numbers, Ocarina's Hyrule Field on PC: the list-writer wait took 142 ms of
every front second before 6229487c8c and still 263 ms/s (1,104 waits/s, test49c) after it; the
d4e8d85d4d dump found every GPU-written list was macro data begun in the entry before (3D 0xe62,
compute 0xe74) and no wait ever found its entry newly GPU-written.

What changes (DmaPusher::Step, the "list writers" site, the largest front wait in
my PS5 timing notes: ~5,100 waits/s, 6.3 ms a frame):
- Unset: before each entry not on GPU-written pages the front waits until the back ran every queued
  dispatch and copy (GpuSplit::WaitForWriters), as before.
- LISTSYNC: GpuSplit::WaitForSyncedWriters waits for min(last writer, last host-level wait). Host-
  level waits are noted (GpuSplit::NoteListSync) at a GP entry's sync bit, the puller WaitForIdle
  and the 3D wait_for_idle (through NoteSync), every syncpoint acquire, every semaphore acquire
  (SemaphoreOperation and SEM_EXECUTE) and every resumed acquire. Fritchii notes only the acquires
  met without a drain; here every acquire is noted however it is met (our SEM_FAST, pending-
  release and same-read paths differ from Fritchii's), which can only add waits.
- LISTSKIP: an entry with dma_state.method_count == 0 skips the wait unless copy engine work the
  back has not run is queued (GpuSplit::NoteCopyWriter, after NoteWriter for MaxwellDMA writers).
  Entries that begin inside a method's data (the parameters compute writes) still wait.
- An entry that did not wait for every writer while a later one was still queued gets a read-only
  check deferred to the back at its ring position (FastDrawNeutral): if one of those writers marked
  its pages GPU-written it logs "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSYNC: command entry at ... was GPU-written by
  work queued before it and read from its submit copy" (first 32, then powers of two). The count
  must stay 0: a line is a stale entry parsed.

Not ported: the removal of EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST (kept as is), EXP41 (our two switches play its
part), any change to the ListGpuWritten wait in ReadGpuWrittenCommands (unchanged, still every
writer), and 266cb620c1's word-level list reads (EXP40) and LIST_VERIFY.

Risk: an entry parsed before a queued writer marked its page reads the CPU's submitted words: a
stale command list can lose the device or hang. Only a page's first GPU write can be missed (the
bit never clears; later entries there take the GPU-written path). LISTSYNC follows the hardware's
fetch ordering; LISTSKIP is Lichii's measured heuristic. With EDEN_UP_OOT_FRONT_WAIT the guest can
run ahead of the back, so a CPU-side wait no longer orders a writer before the next submission's
entries for the front. Cost with a switch on: one Defer (a page-bit read) per entry while writers
are queued. Files: dma_pusher.cpp and engines/puller.cpp (both also compiled as derived copies,
none of the derivation anchors touched), gpu_split.h, gpu_split.cpp.

diff --git a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
index 687f0ab..61ae6cf 100644
--- a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
@@ -436,6 +436,61 @@ static u64 NoteFetchRecheck(GPUVAddr address, u64 words, int mode) {
     return hit;
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSYNC / _LISTSKIP (GpuSplit::ListSyncMode; Frizti/Fritchii 6baafdd7d9, from
+// zortos293/Lichii#805 6229487c8c + d4e8d85d4d): the wait before an entry on pages no GPU work has
+// written yet. Unset: for every queued dispatch and copy, as before. LISTSYNC: for those sent
+// before the last host-level wait. LISTSKIP: an entry that begins between methods
+// (`command_entry`) skips it while no copy engine work is queued (`skipped`). Returns whether any
+// of the work it waited for was still queued.
+static bool WaitForListWriters(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, bool command_entry, bool& skipped) {
+    const int mode = VideoCommon::GpuSplit::ListSyncMode();
+    if (mode == 0) {
+        return split.WaitForWriters();
+    }
+    if (mode >= 2 && command_entry && !split.CopyWritersPending()) {
+        skipped = true;
+        return false;
+    }
+    return split.WaitForSyncedWriters();
+}
+
+// An entry left on its submit copy after WaitForListWriters, with writers sent after what it
+// waited for still queued: the back checks at the entry's place (every writer sent before it has
+// run there) whether one of them marked the entry's pages GPU-written, i.e. whether the full wait
+// would have taken the entry from GPU memory, and logs each one (the count should stay 0). It only
+// reads the page bits. Nothing unless set.
+static void CheckListWriters(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, MemoryManager& memory, GPUVAddr address,
+                             size_t size, bool skipped) {
+    if (VideoCommon::GpuSplit::ListSyncMode() == 0 || size == 0 ||
+        split.Ran(split.LastWriterPosition())) {
+        return;
+    }
+    split.Defer(
+        [memory = &memory, address, size, skipped] {
+            bool written = false;
+            for (GPUVAddr page = address & ~GPUVAddr{0xfff}; !written && page < address + size;
+                 page += 0x1000) {
+                const auto device = memory->GpuToCpuAddress(page);
+                written = device && Nx2IsGpuWritten(*device);
+            }
+            if (!written) {
+                return;
+            }
+            static std::atomic<u32> missed{};
+            const u32 count = missed.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+            if (count <= 32 || (count & (count - 1)) == 0) {
+                LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU,
+                            "EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSYNC: command entry at {:#x} ({} bytes) was "
+                            "GPU-written by work queued before it and read from its submit copy "
+                            "({} so far; {})",
+                            address, size, count,
+                            skipped ? "skipped the wait, LISTSKIP"
+                                    : "waited for the writers before the last sync");
+            }
+        },
+        VideoCommon::GpuSplit::FastDrawNeutral);
+}
+
 bool DmaPusher::WrittenPagesSettled() {
     const u64 marks = Tegra::g_nx2_new_written_pages.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
     const u64 now = static_cast<u64>(Common::g_wall_clock.GetTimeNS().count());
@@ -611,6 +666,11 @@ bool DmaPusher::Step() {
     }
 
     if (header.size > 0) {
+        // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_LISTSYNC: a GP entry with its sync bit is fetched after the work before
